490.4}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "13.5 10.8 11.7 10.6 7.8 9.4 11 12.5 5.7 13.1 11.1 13.8 10.75", "bbox": {"x": 1355.9, "y": 782.0, "width": 60.899999999999864, "height": 407.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "11", "bbox": {"x": 1359.1, "y": 1205.1, "width": 25.59999999999991, "height": 16.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "7.1 15 9.9 11.5 10 16.1 12.8 6.9 11.2 13.8 13.2 10.3 8.9 7.6 15.7 10.4 11.7 12.1", "bbox": {"x": 1355.9, "y": 1233.4, "width": 48.09999999999991, "height": 574.2}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "more significant factor. Amenorrhea - the absence of a menstrual period - occurs among breastfeeding postpartum mothers for a significant period post-birth. Amenorrhea delays the return of ovulation, a biological", "bbox": {"x": 153.7, "y": 1910.7, "width": 657.3999999999999, "height": 137.70000000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "necessity for pregnancy [21]. It is believed that the suckling action inhibits the release of the hormone estradiol, which triggers the return of ovulation [22]. As a result of widespread breastfeeding, postpartum amenorrhea is", "bbox": {"x": 839.8, "y": 1913.1, "width": 657.1000000000001, "height": 135.0}}], "ms": 329.89}